    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup construction is defined by a high-upside core facing exploitable pitching, with **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) leading the charge. **Jackson Merrill** is our strongest play; he benefits from a favorable matchup against Brandon Pfaadt, where a combination of a +12% SP skill boost and a +13% platoon advantage creates a high-ceiling environment. His ability to capitalize on Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which ranks in the 86th percentile for stolen base opportunities\u2014makes him an essential anchor for our pursuit of the scarcity category. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned for a monster day at the #3 spot against McGreevy, where his strong platoon edge against right-handed pitching provides the highest offensive stability in our current rotation.\n\nOur most complex decision centered on the outfield, where **Cole Carrigg** (57.84) held onto a spot despite a challenging matchup against Ian Seymour. While **Cole Carrigg** carries some risk due to Seymour\u2019s 3.49 xERA, the +14% park factor boost provided the necessary cushion to keep him in the lineup over bench alternatives. **Nasim Nunez** (52.94) remains our most precarious start; while he provides necessary stolen base volume, he is facing A. Nola, whose ability to hold runners to a 63% success rate significantly suppresses his efficiency score. We are keeping a close watch on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.07); although his matchup against Cristian Javier carries a slight platoon penalty, the 5.27 xERA of the opposing starter is too appetizing to bench, even if the official lineup order is not yet finalized.\n\nThe bench remains inactive today due to a combination of team off-days and health issues. Our premium assets, including **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jacob Wilson**, are unavailable due to scheduling, while **Jordan Westburg** remains sidelined on the IL. We are monitoring the recovery progress of **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Miguel Vargas** to provide future depth, as our reserve corps\u2014including **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Lara**, and **Denzer Guzman**\u2014are currently held in reserve to preserve our game caps. With no weather-related delays flagged, our primary risk remains the high-strikeout potential of the opposing starters, necessitating a disciplined approach to our SB-heavy strategy.",
